Lab 12: Errata Management and Patching
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand different types of errata (security, bugfix, and enhancement updates)
Identify and analyze available errata using Red Hat Satellite or Foreman/Katello
Apply patches and updates to individual systems and groups of hosts
Schedule automated patch management jobs
Use host collections to manage updates across multiple systems
Verify successful patch deployment and system compliance
Implement best practices for enterprise patch management
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux system administration
Familiarity with Red Hat Enterprise Linux or CentOS/Rocky Linux
Knowledge of package management using yum/dnf
Understanding of system repositories and package sources
Basic command-line navigation skills
Completed previous labs on content management and host registration
