Task 1: Identify Errata in Satellite
Subtask 1.1: Access the Satellite Web Interface
Connect to your Satellite server:

# SSH to your Satellite server (provided in lab environment)
ssh root@satellite.example.com
Verify Satellite services are running:

# Check Satellite status
satellite-maintain service status

# If services are not running, start them
satellite-maintain service start
Access the web interface:

Open your web browser
Navigate to https://satellite.example.com
Login with provided credentials (typically admin/password)
Subtask 1.2: Navigate to Errata Management
Access the Errata section:

In the Satellite web interface, click on Content in the main menu
Select Errata from the dropdown menu
Understand errata types:

Security Errata: Critical security patches (marked with shield icon)
Bugfix Errata: Bug fixes and stability improvements
Enhancement Errata: New features and enhancements
Subtask 1.3: Filter and Analyze Available Errata
Filter errata by type:

# Command-line method to list errata
hammer erratum list --organization "Default Organization"

# Filter by security errata only
hammer erratum list --organization "Default Organization" --errata-type security
View detailed errata information:

# Get details for a specific erratum
hammer erratum info --id RHSA-2023-1234
Check errata applicable to specific hosts:

In the web interface, go to Hosts > All Hosts
Click on a specific host
Navigate to the Errata tab to see applicable updates
Task 2: Apply Updates to Systems via Scheduled Jobs
Subtask 2.1: Prepare for Patch Deployment
Create a maintenance window:

# Set up a maintenance notification
echo "System maintenance scheduled for $(date)" > /etc/motd
Verify host connectivity:

# Test connection to managed hosts
hammer host list --organization "Default Organization"

# Check specific host status
hammer host info --name client1.example.com
Subtask 2.2: Schedule Errata Installation
Schedule updates via web interface:

Navigate to Hosts > All Hosts
Select the target host(s)
Click Select Action > Schedule Remote Job
Choose Install Errata from the job templates
Configure the scheduled job:

Job Template: Install Errata - Katello Script Default
Schedule: Set future date/time for maintenance window
Errata: Select specific errata or choose "All applicable"
Alternative command-line scheduling:

# Schedule errata installation for a specific host
hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Install Errata - Katello Script Default" \
  --search-query "name = client1.example.com" \
  --start-at "2024-01-15 02:00:00" \
  --inputs errata="RHSA-2023-1234,RHBA-2023-5678"
Subtask 2.3: Monitor Job Execution
Track job progress:

# List recent job invocations
hammer job-invocation list

# Get detailed job status
hammer job-invocation info --id JOB_ID
View job output:

In the web interface, go to Monitor > Jobs
Click on the running/completed job
Review the Output tab for detailed execution logs
Verify successful installation:

# Check installed packages on target host
ssh root@client1.example.com "rpm -qa --last | head -20"

# Verify specific security updates
ssh root@client1.example.com "yum history list"
Task 3: Test Patch Management for Multiple Hosts Using Host Collections
Subtask 3.1: Create Host Collections
Create a host collection via web interface:

Navigate to Hosts > Host Collections
Click Create Host Collection
Name: Production Servers
Description: Critical production systems requiring coordinated patching
Create host collection via command line:

# Create a new host collection
hammer host-collection create \
  --name "Development Servers" \
  --description "Development environment systems" \
  --organization "Default Organization"
Add hosts to collections:

# Add multiple hosts to a collection
hammer host-collection add-host \
  --name "Production Servers" \
  --host-ids 1,2,3,4 \
  --organization "Default Organization"
Subtask 3.2: Apply Patches to Host Collections
Install errata on host collection:

# Apply all security errata to a host collection
hammer host-collection erratum install \
  --name "Production Servers" \
  --errata "RHSA-2023-1234,RHSA-2023-5678" \
  --organization "Default Organization"
Schedule bulk updates:

# Schedule updates for entire host collection
hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Install Errata - Katello Script Default" \
  --search-query "host_collection = \"Production Servers\"" \
  --start-at "2024-01-15 03:00:00" \
  --inputs errata="security"
Subtask 3.3: Implement Staged Rollout Strategy
Create staging groups:

# Create collections for staged deployment
hammer host-collection create --name "Patch Group 1" --organization "Default Organization"
hammer host-collection create --name "Patch Group 2" --organization "Default Organization"
hammer host-collection create --name "Patch Group 3" --organization "Default Organization"
Distribute hosts across groups:

# Add 25% of hosts to Group 1 (early adopters)
hammer host-collection add-host --name "Patch Group 1" --host-ids 1,2

# Add 50% of hosts to Group 2 (main deployment)
hammer host-collection add-host --name "Patch Group 2" --host-ids 3,4,5,6

# Add remaining hosts to Group 3 (final wave)
hammer host-collection add-host --name "Patch Group 3" --host-ids 7,8
Execute staged deployment:

# Stage 1: Deploy to early adopters
hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Install Errata - Katello Script Default" \
  --search-query "host_collection = \"Patch Group 1\"" \
  --start-at "2024-01-15 01:00:00"

# Stage 2: Deploy to main group (after validation)
hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Install Errata - Katello Script Default" \
  --search-query "host_collection = \"Patch Group 2\"" \
  --start-at "2024-01-15 02:00:00"

# Stage 3: Deploy to remaining systems
hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Install Errata - Katello Script Default" \
  --search-query "host_collection = \"Patch Group 3\"" \
  --start-at "2024-01-15 03:00:00"
Subtask 3.4: Validate Patch Deployment
Create validation script:

# Create a post-patch validation script
cat > /tmp/patch_validation.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

echo "=== Patch Validation Report ==="
echo "Host: $(hostname)"
echo "Date: $(date)"
echo

echo "=== Recently Installed Packages ==="
rpm -qa --last | head -10
echo

echo "=== System Uptime ==="
uptime
echo

echo "=== Critical Services Status ==="
systemctl is-active sshd httpd chronyd
echo

echo "=== Available Security Updates ==="
yum --security check-update 2>/dev/null | grep -i security || echo "No security updates available"
echo

echo "=== Disk Space ==="
df -h / /var /tmp
EOF

chmod +x /tmp/patch_validation.sh
Run validation across host collections:

# Execute validation script on all patched systems
hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Run Command - Script Default" \
  --search-query "host_collection = \"Production Servers\"" \
  --inputs command="/tmp/patch_validation.sh"
Generate compliance report:

# Check errata compliance status
hammer host list --search "errata_status = security_needed" \
  --organization "Default Organization"

# Generate detailed compliance report
hammer report-template generate \
  --name "Host - Errata Report" \
  --organization "Default Organization"
