Emergency Patch Deployment
Rapid security patch deployment:
# Emergency security patch script
cat > /usr/local/bin/emergency_patch.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

ERRATUM_ID=$1
HOST_COLLECTION=$2

if [ -z "$ERRATUM_ID" ] || [ -z "$HOST_COLLECTION" ]; then
    echo "Usage: $0 <erratum_id> <host_collection>"
    exit 1
fi

echo "Deploying emergency patch $ERRATUM_ID to $HOST_COLLECTION"

hammer job-invocation create \
  --job-template "Install Errata - Katello Script Default" \
  --search-query "host_collection = \"$HOST_COLLECTION\"" \
  --inputs errata="$ERRATUM_ID" \
  --start-at "now"
EOF

chmod +x /usr/local/bin/emergency_patch.sh
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Errata Installation Failures
Problem: Patches fail to install on some hosts

Solution:

# Check host connectivity
hammer host list --search "last_checkin < \"1 hour ago\""

# Verify repository synchronization
hammer repository list --organization "Default Organization" | grep -i "sync.*success"

# Check client registration status
ssh root@problematic-host "subscription-manager status"
Issue 2: Scheduling Conflicts
Problem: Multiple patch jobs conflict with each other

Solution:

# List active and scheduled jobs
hammer job-invocation list --search "state = running OR state = scheduled"

# Cancel conflicting jobs if necessary
hammer job-invocation cancel --id CONFLICTING_JOB_ID
Issue 3: Host Collection Management Issues
Problem: Hosts not responding to collection-based commands

Solution:

# Verify host collection membership
hammer host-collection hosts --name "Production Servers"

# Check individual host status
hammer host info --name problematic-host.example.com

# Re-register problematic hosts
ssh root@problematic-host "subscription-manager clean && subscription-manager register"
